=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  Data sources (web useTranslation + useSettings + useFormatting + useUnits): collapsed
  into the P1/S8 CostSavingsSnapshot (derived CostSavingsConfig + SI CostSavingsInputs)
  delivered through CostSavingsSource→CostSavingsModel. No HTTP / no hook calls in the view.
  Render math (verbatim from source):
    - energyKwh = stats.energyWh / 1000 ; tripCost = evCost = energyKwh * costPerKwh
    - costPerDistanceUnit = (energyKwh*costPerKwh) / convertDistanceFromSI(distanceM, unit)
      (nil when distanceM<=0)  [web useFormatting.costPerDistanceUnit]
    - estimateGasCost: nil when mpg<=0||gasPrice<=0||distanceM<=0; else
      (distanceM→mi)/mpg * gasPrice, × 3.78541 when gas_unit==liter  [web estimateGasCost]
    - savings = gasCost==nil ? nil : gasCost - evCost
  Settings defaults reproduced: base_cost_per_kwh ?? 0.12 ; currency_symbol||'$'
  (untrimmed-when-trim-nonempty) ; floor(decimal_precision) if finite&>=0 else 2 ;
  unit_of_length('mi'|'km') ; gas_efficiency_mpg ?? 0 ; gas_price_per_unit ?? 0 ;
  gas_unit ?? 'gallon' ; locale||'en-US'. Constants: 1609.344 m/mi, 1000 m/km, 3.78541 gal→L.
  Cells (web grid, render order + visibility branches):
    1. Trip Cost  (always)            value formatEnergyCost(energyWh/1000) — green ;
                                      sub "at {sym}{rate}/kWh"
    2. Cost / {unit} (distanceM>0)    value formatCurrency(costPerDistanceUnit ?? 0, 3) — cyan
    3. Gas Cost (equiv) (savings>0)   value formatCurrency(gasCost) — red ; sub "at {mpg} MPG"
    4. vs Gas Savings   (savings>0)   value formatCurrency(savings) — emerald
    5. Savings %        (savings>0)   value fmtNumber(savings/gasCost*100, 0)+"%" — emerald
  i18n keys (referenced==declared, verified by cross-check; table "CostSavingsPanel"):
    driveDetail.costSavings/tripCost/atRate/costPerUnit/gasCostEquiv/atMpg/gasSavings/savingsPct
    + native chrome costSavings.{live,stale,offline,staleBanner,offlineBanner,refresh,
    loadingA11y,empty,errorTitle,retry}. No English literals in Swift. i18next {{name}} →
    positional String(format:) %@ / %1$@%2$@.
  States (every one renders): loading (skeleton grid) / empty (degenerate drive, no
  energy+no distance → ContentUnavailableView) / error (QueryError peer + retry) / data ;
  orthogonal connection axis live/stale/offline → freshness chip + banner + one-shot
  auto-refresh on the stale transition.
  Accessibility: header isHeader trait ; each cell is one combined element with a
  "{label}, {value}[, {detail}]" VoiceOver label ; refresh/retry labelled ; Dynamic Type
